# 2026-10-06: the FILE FRAMING around struct Game, checked since the
# 2026-09-28 sync slipped a change past the line above. Upstream's replay
# rewrite (#5353) turned `struct FileChunkHeader`'s three `unsigned long`s
# into uint32_t. On upstream's 32-bit Windows build nothing changed; on 64-bit
# Linux every chunk header went from 24 bytes to 12, struct Game did not move,
# and so this check stayed green while builds 5751..5768 read every older save
# as an empty slot (its info block failed the id check) -- hidden from Load,
# listed as "Unused", and overwritable from the save menu. read_chunk_header()
# in src/game_saves.c now reads both layouts and writes the 12-byte one. These
# two lines make any further framing change fail here instead of in players'
# save folders.
# (was) sizeof_chunk_header=12
# (was) sizeof_catalogue_entry=412

# 2026-10-10: the fork's own fix, not an upstream sync. 53383086 -> 53317550.
# `struct ScriptValue` (src/lvl_script.h), saved as
# `script.values[SCRIPT_VALUES_COUNT]` (2048) inside `struct Game`, declared
# its `longs[8]`/`ulongs[8]` union members as `long`: 4 bytes on upstream's
# 32-bit Windows build, 8 here, so the union was 64 bytes instead of 32 and
# the level-script commands that pack shorts and bytes next to a long slot by
# index overlapped differently than upstream (ADD_EFFECT_GENERATOR_TO_LEVEL,
# CREATE_EFFECTS_LINE, DISPLAY_VARIABLE_WITH_LABEL, ...). They are int32_t and
# uint32_t now, as on Windows: 69 -> 37 bytes per value, x2048 = -65536.
# Accepted deliberately by the owner: the alternative is keeping a script
# value layout that silently runs level scripts wrong; saves from earlier
# builds will not load.

